WEBVTT

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:02.340
The Letter of Marque...

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.150
The letter itself is passed down,

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.770
just with a new name and date written inside.

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:09.440
After an endless mountain of paperwork, Kato Marika

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.440
has succeeded in earning the right to become captain

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.150
of the space pirate ship Bentenmaru.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.990
However, this is only the start of what she must do

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.660
to be recognized by others as a pirate captain.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.410
Stay strong, Kato Marika!

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.370
Fight, Kato Marika!

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.250
Space awaits you.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.290
It's Marika... Here I go!

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.270
Your goal here is recon.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.360
Keep your data lines and radio channels open at all times.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:11.480
Roger.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:14.610
But if we get into a battle, I'll have you shut them both down.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.280
Yeah, gladly.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.740
How's the probe looking?

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:19.820
No problems.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:22.080
It's transmitting the information.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.840
What are you playing around for?

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:34.630
There's something fishy about this plant.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.050
Auto-programmed tugboats, huh?

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:41.590
There's nothing on the radar.

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:42.220
But...

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:47.730
I knew it!

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.770
I found the enemy on the other side of the planet.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.020
Stealth, huh?

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.530
No wonder they didn't appear on radar.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:57.650
We see them too.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.820
Captain, return to base.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:00.530
Roger.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:03.950
If I don't return soon, the Bentenmaru will be in danger!

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.760
This is really, really bad!

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.510
Seriously bad!

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.650
Calm down.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.110
Think.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:49.580
Calm down... Calm down... Calm down...

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.870
This isn't the time to be calm, Marika.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.920
Did I get shot down?

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.920
Your pencil box did.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:03.050
A dream, huh?

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.640
That's a relief...

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.220
Jeez.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:09.020
Look. Homeroom's over.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.270
The teacher felt bad, and didn't wake you up.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.850
He said to come to the nurse's office once you woke up.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.020
Why the nurse's office?

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:20.610
I know I may not be the one to talk,

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:23.450
but are you okay, Captain?

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.200
Well...

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.370
Your grades have been falling since the second semester began.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:33.370
You were doing well before, so you aren't failing yet, but...

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:38.500
Lately, all your quiz scores have been F's.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.630
Even if they were pop quizzes, that's...

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.010
Well...

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.220
Sorry.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:48.010
We won't do anything too hard while our captain's still in school.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:52.430
We're trying to choose jobs that we can complete in a single day.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.390
But if doing both is too hard, then you should consider dropping—

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:56.440
I'm not dropping out of school!

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:59.230
I'm going to graduate!

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:00.530
I'm just fine!

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:01.320
I'll try harder!

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.610
There are times when trying harder isn't enough.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.120
I can decide that for myself!

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.240
And I will!

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.280
So, please...

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.920
She's the one doing the studying.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:18.920
I guess the change in circumstances has been hard on her.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:22.300
She used to always be on time and have perfect attendance,

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.630
but now she comes late and leaves early almost every day.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:26.220
We can't do anything about it.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.510
We can't take any big jobs.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.850
That means taking more small ones.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.430
She says she'll make the decision for herself, huh?

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:38.860
That's natural for a captain, but...

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:40.570
She's a first year high school student.

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:42.650
But she's a pirate.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:46.240
And all that matters for a pirate is winning in the end.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.700
This is training too.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.910
To become an adult.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:54.000
I wonder what her obsession is with high school though.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.300
Thank you!
Lamp House

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.340
The Lamp House is great.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:09.680
It calms me down.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.010
Yeah, I bet the manager would be happy to hear that.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:16.810
I heard we won't be doing any pirating for a while.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:18.600
I have to redeem myself.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.440
Redeem?

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.690
Then why not study?

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:25.570
Haven't your test scores been horrendous lately?

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.740
My job here is important too.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:39.920
Welcome.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.250
Huh?

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:41.960
Chiaki?

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.300
Not this again...

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:47.760
Here you go.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.760
Everyone was surprised when

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.850
you transferred at the start of the second semester.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:56.810
Sorry I didn't come to say hi.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.270
Looking for Marika?

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:02.730
I knew it.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.020
Sorry.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:05.650
She was here a second ago,

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:07.360
but I guess she had a job to do...

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.240
No way.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.200
She wasn't supposed to have any work this week.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:13.910
I knew you came to see her!

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.330
N-No...

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.200
I came to eat this parfait.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.830
My shift's almost over.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.120
Want to come with me afterwards?

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:26.050
Here's the data from Hyakume.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:27.510
Contract

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.510
Weren't we not supposed to have any work this week?

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:34.720
It's a sudden job, so we get up-front payment plus a big bonus.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:36.470
Twice the normal rate.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.060
We'll take it!

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:42.600
It's the usual pirate job on a luxury liner.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:45.140
But this time, the client added an optional package, so be careful.

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:46.480
Optional package?

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.530
We're almost at the Bentenmaru.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:56.830
Marika works really hard.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:58.660
People only look at the results,

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.620
so they all treat her like a genius.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:01.960
But you know the truth.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:05.460
Yeah. She pushes herself really close to the limit.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:13.590
Back in middle school, I once asked her

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:16.260
why she works so hard at everything.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:21.230
And she said she wanted to know more about Ririka.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.730
Even though that's her own mother.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:27.480
I was like, "Huh?"

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.440
But when I went to her house, I understood.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:33.110
Her mom's amazing!

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:35.320
I know that.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:36.910
Blaster Ririka.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.450
She's a legendary female pirate.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.830
So I heard.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:46.750
But it wasn't an old story like that...

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:48.040
When I met her,

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:51.130
she was like so amazing, I didn't know what to do.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:54.340
When you're near her, it's just overpowering.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.220
She's huge!

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.810
Huge?

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:04.600
Yeah... As a person.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.640
You mean she's a great person?

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:06.650
Yeah, that's it.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:11.940
And so, her mom's like this big mountain, and Marika doesn't want to climb it.

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:14.610
She wants to be another big mountain next to her.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:17.870
Yeah, that's it. I'm sure of it.

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:20.490
What? That doesn't make any sense.

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:21.330
That's true.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.380
See you then.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.040
Thanks for coming with me.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:32.760
What were you trying to say, anyway?

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.470
I don't know.

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:36.930
Just seeing your face

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:39.470
made me feel like talking, Chiaki.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:41.560
I told you, don't call me that.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:44.560
Bye!

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:47.520
In space, you're taking over my place.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:48.310
Thanks.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:50.400
Who's taking your place?

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.530
Thanks, huh?

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:06.460
Captain... Captain...

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.710
Please report to the bridge immediately.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:09.810
Captain!

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:16.920
Right!

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:24.770
Sorry I'm late.

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:25.520
You're late.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.600
But these clothes take forever to put on!

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.600
I can make some adjustments, right?

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:31.980
Whatever.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:35.320
Just do it after this job is over.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.440
Is there still time?

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:39.700
One minute, thirty seconds until we return to normal space.

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:41.820
Let's go over this once more.

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:47.080
Our target is the Frigard Line's mega-ship, the Symphony Angel.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:51.040
It has a three-ship escort, so we'll be using ship-to-ship combat before boarding.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:53.040
That's the optional package the client chose, right?

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:55.460
We're vastly more powerful than they are.

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:59.050
We knock them around a bit, and then we demand their surrender.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.930
Once we've boarded, we do our pirating as usual.

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:06.390
Have we had our meeting with them?

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.640
We took care of that before you guys arrived.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.270
Our plan for the optional ship-to-ship battle,

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.610
including surprise attack, has been filed with

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.610
the Navigation Control Bureau and has been passed along to the client as well.

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:21.700
They want to show their customers something like a real battle, huh?

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:25.080
Okay, everyone.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:26.450
Time to get to work.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:28.950
Returning to normal space.

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:54.100
Target confirmed.

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:56.700
Angel-class mega-liner

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.690
and three Corback-class escorts.

00:11:59.140 --> 00:11:59.940
All ready?

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.540
Radar and sensors are all green.

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:05.120
Propulsion and mobility systems are all green.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.240
We can fire at will.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.460
Electronic warfare systems are operational.

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:12.370
Weapon and navigation systems are ready for battle.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:14.800
The Corbacks have sighted us.

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:18.050
They have our position and transponder.

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:22.600
They've confirmed our name and position.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:24.760
Bentenmaru, let's go.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.220
Launching the Bentenmaru.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:29.930
Initiating jamming too.

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:46.250
I have all three escorts.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:48.410
Hm...

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:52.460
After the electronic warfare, we approach and begin ship-to-ship combat.

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:54.330
Then we approach the Symphony Angel.

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:57.590
Nothing for me to do until we board.

00:12:57.590 --> 00:12:58.960
Remember to send the surrender demand.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:00.600
Sending.

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:02.560
So, they'll attack soon.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:04.720
Energy readings in enemy ships rising.

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:07.180
They're serious.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.940
They ignored our surrender demand?

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:12.680
Why does everyone love firing their guns so much?

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:15.530
You don't get many chances at real combat.

00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:17.490
They're paying top dollar.

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:19.150
Let them have their fun.

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:21.240
We have the targeting data.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:24.400
We'll wait for the Corbacks to open fire, and then respond.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:26.860
Okay, here they come!

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:32.840
Yes, I bought them, Dad.

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:35.630
Jasmine tea and your favorite, shochu.

00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:37.840
I sent them by space post earlier.

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:40.300
All that's left are the duty-free pickled plums, right?

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:42.420
What?

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.760
I can't hear you.

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:49.770
Understood, Captain.

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:52.150
I'll remain here.

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:54.180
Send me the information once you get it.

00:13:58.610 --> 00:14:01.520
Something's happening.

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:02.610
Huh?

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:03.400
Huh? Huh?

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.820
The Corbacks have changed attack pattern.

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:07.290
What?

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:09.670
They've stopped the brute-force electronic warfare

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:12.710
and are maintaining formation while they split up.

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:15.130
Can anyone tell me what this means?

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:17.050
Go, Kato Marika.

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:19.510
Huh? Um...

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:23.470
I think they're increasing their scanning capability by widening the gap

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:26.050
between the network-connected sensors.

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:27.220
That's right.

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:30.890
Will they be able to find our present location?

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:35.610
Mass-produced shipboard computers aren't fast enough. Don't worry.

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:40.280
The amount of sensor data increases at an insane rate,

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:43.120
so just analyzing it will take all their processing power.

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:47.690
Unless one decides to take a chance and focus their sensors, we're fine.

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:50.710
Anyone with that kind of guts would be a pirate.

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:51.870
Yup, yup.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:52.710
I can see it.

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:56.170
What can you see, Luca?

00:14:56.170 --> 00:14:57.670
I can't say.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:14:58.830
Right, right.

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:01.760
Now, let's finish this.

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:04.290
I have school tomorrow.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:08.760
Enemy Corbacks designated as Alpha, Bravo, and Charlie.

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:10.560
Firing data input.

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:11.970
Ready to fire warning shots.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:12.930
Fire.

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:17.520
All three have stopped.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:18.400
Okay!

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:19.280
Not yet.

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:20.900
The electronic warfare is still going on!

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:24.110
Enemy ship energy readings are rising.

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:25.370
They're gonna fire again.

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:26.530
They won't surrender?

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:29.790
Don't worry.

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:31.160
They're still far off.

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:36.740
They've shifted from a simultaneous firing pattern to a wave-based one.

00:15:37.210 --> 00:15:39.620
What hasn't changed is how bad their targeting is though.

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:47.300
Maybe I'll turn the alarms off.

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:48.010
No.

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:51.890
No matter how bad they are, an attack is an attack.

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:55.150
It doesn't change the fact that they're shooting at the Bentenmaru.

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:56.720
You can't relax your guard.

00:15:58.820 --> 00:16:02.390
Hey, do you think they might not have received the surrender order?

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:05.360
That message had a receipt confirmation.

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:08.400
If their comms people aren't slacking off, they got it.

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:11.900
It's possible to simultaneously surround all three ships with cannon fire.

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:14.210
Let's show them whom they're dealing with.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.000
That's right.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:18.410
Our customers are watching.

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:20.380
We need to give them their money's worth.

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:21.870
Roger.

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:25.290
Targeting Alpha, Bravo, Charlie.

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:27.250
Firing all cannons.

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:32.670
Send another surrender order.

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:37.900
Add that our next shot will be a warning shot targeting the Symphony Angel.

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:38.730
Roger.

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:42.940
These decisions are the captain's job too.

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:43.850
Learn it soon.

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:48.530
I don't like threatening them...

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:49.820
We're pirates.

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:52.080
The scarier the better.

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:54.200
And this isn't a threat.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.250
It's a bargaining tactic.

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.790
Main cannon is charging.

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:00.740
If it's just a warning shot, we can fire immediately.

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:02.880
We've got an answer.

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:06.880
But it's from the Symphony Angel, not its escorts.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:09.000
"We surrender."

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.890
The ship that's being protected surrendered?

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:13.970
Isn't that the wrong progression?

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:17.600
Shouldn't the escorts surrender before the luxury liner?

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:21.980
The escort fleet just surrendered too.

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:26.190
Um... This one's in the name of the fleet commander.

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:28.910
Surrenders from two places?

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:29.870
Did they make a mistake?

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:32.940
People make mistakes all the time.

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:36.160
But while you can always speculate,

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:39.620
if you always interpret things in the way that's convenient, it'll bite you in the end.

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:43.370
What are the escorts doing?

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:45.630
They've dropped out of battle formation.

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:49.880
Their energy readings are still a bit high, but that isn't uncommon.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:53.380
I have the Symphony Angel's control systems.

00:17:57.310 --> 00:17:59.390
Coorie, continue electronic warfare.

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:01.770
The Bentenmaru will dock with the target.

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:03.900
Boarding teams, get ready.

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:07.190
It's time for some piracy!

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:20.460
Got all your valuables ready?

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:23.240
Hand them over!

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:30.760
I got really into it again...

00:18:32.430 --> 00:18:36.090
I think I'm getting into it more each time I do it.

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:39.270
Is this really a good idea?

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:48.570
But you decided you'd do both,

00:18:48.570 --> 00:18:49.770
right, Kato Marika?

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:51.610
Okay!

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:01.620
Now, then...

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:03.670
Time to study for tomorrow.

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:07.830
Coming.

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:09.840
Yes, this is Marika.

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:12.430
Hey, it's Hyakume.

00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:14.850
Sorry to bother you when you're relaxing,

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:17.680
but can you come to the bridge?

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:20.900
From the way you're talking, has something happened?

00:19:22.690 --> 00:19:24.350
Just get up here.

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:25.560
And wear your uniform!

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:28.940
Hurry!

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:32.310
Right! Right!

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:33.980
A stowaway?

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:34.990
When?

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:35.740
From where?

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:37.030
How?

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:39.870
A stowaway boarded our pirate ship?

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:42.040
What kind of bad joke is that?

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:43.700
It's true.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.000
When?

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:47.880
During our piracy.

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:50.420
They snuck on board from the Symphony Angel.

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:51.920
Um...

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:55.090
When we docked with the Symphony Angel and

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:58.510
changed our control from wireless to local,

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:00.800
I thought there was some weird noise.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:06.150
It didn't worry me because it didn't trigger any of our security systems, but...

00:20:06.150 --> 00:20:11.520
It looks like they temporarily overwrote the Bentenmaru's security systems...

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:15.360
But it's fine now.

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:16.910
It's back to normal.

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:20.790
I confirmed it when we undocked...

00:20:20.790 --> 00:20:24.830
No traces remained in the observation cameras or sensors.

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:28.580
Doesn't that just mean their hacking was that good?

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:31.630
I told you...

00:20:31.630 --> 00:20:32.910
You told us nothing!

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:36.300
And so, we had you come here.

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:39.130
Do we have to worry about explosives?

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:42.220
The dangerous materials sensor isn't picking up anything.

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:43.590
We shouldn't have to worry.

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:46.550
Energy signals and metal signals are within normal parameters.

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:49.510
It doesn't appear they brought anything bad on board.

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:53.240
So this stowaway... Where are they, and what are they doing?

00:20:53.240 --> 00:20:56.910
They snuck into docking control, and have holed-up there.

00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:58.200
What about the sleeping gas?

00:20:58.200 --> 00:20:59.440
Why aren't we using it?

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.400
About that...

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:09.420
Estimated height 140 cm?

00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:11.380
Weight 34 kg?!

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:14.670
Given the fact that we don't see any

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:18.550
mechanical or electronic noise in their energy signal,

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:21.590
our stowaway is likely to be an ordinary child.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:23.220
An ordinary child?

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:25.050
What does the kid want?

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.560
They're just hiding.

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:30.760
The only thing they said was they demand to speak with the captain.

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:33.980
So we called you.

00:21:39.530 --> 00:21:40.660
Very well.

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:41.440
Connect me.

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:45.540
This is the Bentenmaru's bridge.

00:21:45.540 --> 00:21:47.660
Docking control, can you hear me?

00:21:49.210 --> 00:21:52.410
I want to speak with the captain.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.830
I want to speak with the captain.

00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:58.290
I won't negotiate with anyone else.

00:22:00.470 --> 00:22:01.800
You were right...

00:22:02.470 --> 00:22:04.100
That's a child's voice.

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:08.300
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:11.470
The Peace Does Not Last
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:12.510
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:18.020
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:21.020
Welcome glory, let's breakthrough and fly out now, let's go!

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:24.400
Run towards an unlimited dimension. Come, let's accelerate beyond this

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:27.490
history that's to be known, regardless of time. Fly towards a destined future.

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:30.530
Just a fossil if you give up a miracle. Your decision is your best choice.

00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:39.460
There's another, unknown, me hiding in my heart.

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:44.340
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:44.630 --> 00:22:48.170
How far?

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:50.840
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell! Go, go, ring, ring a bell!

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:54.470
Until the end.

00:22:54.470 --> 00:22:55.810
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell!

00:22:55.810 --> 00:22:59.140
You're lost and missing.

00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:07.990
We're lost without a hope of any shelter.

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:11.740
But why? What did we do? What did we do?

00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:13.160
What should we do?

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:16.330
From the world beyond shadows invade.

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:20.620
We're destined to stop them with our lives.

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:26.670
So no matter where we go, as far as it takes

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:30.930
we'll always believe in ourselves.

00:23:39.310 --> 00:23:41.270
Gale winds blow from a foreign land.

00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:44.310
How will the girl captain decide to deal

00:23:44.310 --> 00:23:46.940
with her tiny, but noble, stowaway?

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:49.070
The two girls meet,

00:23:49.950 --> 00:23:53.320
and the sealed darkness of history begins to move once more.

00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:56.120
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:56.120 --> 00:23:57.540
The princess and the pirate.

00:23:57.540 --> 00:23:59.000
Look forward to it.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:05.000
The Princess and the Pirate

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:10.390
There are times when trying harder isn't enough.
